# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`. Without a .dockerignore that copies the
# ENTIRE working tree into the image. Verified on 2026-08-20 by building
# `--target production` and inspecting the result:
#
#   /code/.env   5205 bytes   <- present
#   /code        877 MB       <- frontend/node_modules + frontend/.next
#
# Two separate problems, both serious for a registry-hosted deploy (Render,
# Railway, anything that stores the built image):
#
#   1. SECRETS SHIPPED. .env holds the live ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, SECRET_KEY and
#      ENCRYPTION_KEY. Anyone who can pull or inspect the image has them, and
#      image layers persist after the file is "deleted" in a later layer.
#
#   2. SILENT CONFIG FALLBACK, which is the subtler one. pydantic-settings
#      reads .env when a variable is absent from the environment. Real env vars
#      win, so the dashboard still governs whatever it sets — but anything the
#      dashboard FORGETS silently falls back to the development value instead
#      of failing. A production container could quietly point DATABASE_URL at
#      localhost:5433 or boot with the dev SECRET_KEY, and
#      app/core/production_guard.py would see a populated value and pass.
#      Excluding .env makes a missing variable an immediate, loud failure.
#
# Rule of thumb: if it is generated, secret, or only used on a developer's
# machine, it does not belong in the image.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never in an image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend build artefacts and dependencies (~820 MB of the 877 MB above).
# The API image never runs the frontend; Vercel builds it from source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
frontend/.vercel/
frontend/android/
**/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python caches and local venvs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VCS and editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime state — logs, schedules, scratch. Celery beat recreates its
# schedule file; shipping a stale one confuses the scheduler.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.runlogs/
.phasec/
logs/
*.log
celerybeat-schedule*
media/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs and local-only compose files. Keep the image to what runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
